  <revision rev="9" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>e035393b2ef95bc9d3825a9df854a9d3</srcmd5>
    <version>2.5.2</version>
    <time>1785944939</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to version 2.5.2

Upstream: gpsd support for more recent versions (#404), second rig not
connecting (#407), a data race fixed by reloading satellites in the main
thread (#409), warning messages at exit, and an MSYS64 compile fix.

Packaging: drops the obsolete Group tag. spec-cleaner clean, builds green on
Tumbleweed aarch64 with rpmlint 0 errors 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1369550</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="10" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>259eb2f9c4730e97055eb83f91757f30</srcmd5>
    <version>2.6</version>
    <time>1787767059</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to gpredict 2.6 plus a spec cleanup.

Upstream 2.6 adds a satellite filter to the radio and rotator controllers,
removes the NOAA and Molniya satellite groups (no longer available) and
invalid data from satellites.dat, and fixes several polar-view defects
(North/South label positioning, cursor elevation, the missing Next Event
entry, and the orientation setting shown in the config dialog).

Packaging changes:
- Dropped the build dependency on goocanvas-3.0. It is unused since 2.5
  replaced goocanvas with native GTK3/Cairo drawing; the string does not
  occur anywhere in the source tree any more.
- Dropped the build dependency on libtool. The release tarball is a real
  &quot;make dist&quot; artifact that ships configure, Makefile.in and ltmain.sh,
  and nothing regenerates them during the build.
- Dropped the -fcommon workaround; the package builds without it and the
  full optflags set still reaches every compile line.
- Declared the minimal versions configure actually tests for, so OBS holds
  the package unresolvable rather than starting a build that can only die
  in configure: intltool &gt;= 0.21, gtk+-3.0 &gt;= 3.0 and libgps &gt;= 2.90.
- Stopped shipping the upstream ChangeLog, which is now a one-line stub
  pointing at NEWS.
- Corrected the License tag from GPL-2.0-only to
  GPL-2.0-or-later AND LGPL-3.0-or-later. All 123 licence-bearing upstream
  sources grant &quot;version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any later
  version&quot; and upstream's own AppStream metainfo declares GPL-2.0+; the
  bundled src/nxjson is listed in gpredict_SOURCES and therefore compiled
  into the gpredict binary under LGPL-3.0-or-later. The derivation is
  recorded as a Legal-Review-Notice comment above the tag.

Built locally on aarch64 and on OBS for Tumbleweed x86_64/aarch64; rpmlint
is unchanged from 2.5.2 (0 errors, 0 badness).</comment>
    <requestid>1373839</requestid>
  </revision>
